Third-party software
------------------------------------------------------------------------

qmesh is designed to compose with the broader 2026 quantum software
ecosystem. The following projects are *optional* runtime dependencies; their
licenses apply only when the user chooses to install and load them.

  * Qiskit / Qiskit Aer .................................. Apache-2.0
      (IBM Quantum, https://github.com/Qiskit)
  * Cirq ................................................. Apache-2.0
      (Google Quantum AI, https://github.com/quantumlib/Cirq)
  * PennyLane ............................................ Apache-2.0
      (Xanadu, https://github.com/PennyLaneAI/pennylane)
  * Pulser / pulser-simulation ........................... Apache-2.0
      (Pasqal, https://github.com/pasqal-io/Pulser)
  * Strawberry Fields .................................... Apache-2.0
      (Xanadu, https://github.com/XanaduAI/strawberryfields)
  * MrMustard ............................................ Apache-2.0
      (Xanadu, https://github.com/XanaduAI/MrMustard)
  * Bloqade .............................................. Apache-2.0
      (QuEra, https://github.com/QuEraComputing/bloqade-python)
  * pytket / TKET ........................................ Apache-2.0
      (Quantinuum, https://github.com/CQCL/tket)
  * BQSKit ............................................... BSD-3-Clause
      (LBNL, https://github.com/BQSKit/bqskit)
  * MQT Core ............................................. MIT
      (TU Munich, https://github.com/cda-tum/mqt-core)
  * Mitiq ................................................ GPL-3.0
      (Unitary Fund, https://github.com/unitaryfoundation/mitiq).
      qmesh links to Mitiq dynamically only when the user opts in via the
      `[mitiq]` extra; qmesh itself does not include any Mitiq source.
  * Stim ................................................. Apache-2.0
      (Google Quantum AI, https://github.com/quantumlib/Stim)
  * PyMatching ........................................... Apache-2.0
      (https://github.com/oscarhiggott/PyMatching)
  * Amazon Braket SDK .................................... Apache-2.0
      (AWS, https://github.com/aws/amazon-braket-sdk-python)
  * CUDA-Q ............................................... Apache-2.0
      (NVIDIA, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-quantum)
  * OpenQASM 3 reference parser .......................... Apache-2.0
  * NumPy ................................................ BSD-3-Clause
  * Pydantic ............................................. MIT
  * cryptography ......................................... Apache-2.0 / BSD
  * Rich, Typer .......................................... MIT
  * FastAPI, Uvicorn, SQLAlchemy ......................... MIT / BSD
  * PyTorch .............................................. BSD-style
  * Outlines ............................................. Apache-2.0

The list above tracks the runtime dependencies declared in pyproject.toml
at the time of release. It is informational; consult each project for the
authoritative license text.

